/*!
\page page_stpxlHitCollection StPxlHitCollection — Collection Documentation

\ref StPxlHitCollection is the top-level container for all reconstructed Pixel
Detector (PXL) hits in a single STAR event.  The PXL was the innermost layer of
the STAR Heavy Flavour Tracker (HFT), providing high-resolution silicon pixel
measurements for heavy-flavour vertex tagging.  Hits are organised in a
four-level hierarchy: detector → sector → ladder → sensor.

\see StPxlHitCollection
\see StPxlSectorHitCollection
\see StPxlLadderHitCollection
\see StPxlSensorHitCollection
\see StPxlHit

---

\section pxl_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
StPxlHitCollection                   (top-level, one per event)
└── StPxlSectorHitCollection           [10 sectors, indices 0–9]
    └── StPxlLadderHitCollection         [4 ladders per sector, indices 0–3]
        └── StPxlSensorHitCollection       [10 sensors per ladder, indices 0–9]
            └── StSPtrVecPxlHit              (owns the StPxlHit objects)
\endcode

All sub-collection nodes are embedded (stack-allocated) inside their parent;
no heap allocation is used for collection nodes.

\section pxl_containment Containment Model

| Level    | Class                          | Contents                                    |
|----------|--------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Detector | \ref StPxlHitCollection        | 10 \ref StPxlSectorHitCollection objects    |
| Sector   | \ref StPxlSectorHitCollection  | 4 \ref StPxlLadderHitCollection objects     |
| Ladder   | \ref StPxlLadderHitCollection  | 10 \ref StPxlSensorHitCollection objects    |
| Sensor   | \ref StPxlSensorHitCollection  | `StSPtrVecPxlHit` of `StPxlHit*`            |

\section pxl_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StPxlSensorHitCollection holds its hits in a member of type
\c StSPtrVecPxlHit, which is a **smart-pointer vector** that **owns** the
\ref StPxlHit objects it contains.  The \ref StPxlSensorHitCollection destructor
explicitly deletes every hit in the vector (necessary because \ref StPxlHit
provides its own pool-allocated \c new/delete).

All intermediate sub-collection arrays are embedded members of their parent
classes and are destroyed automatically with the parent.
\ref StPxlHitCollection itself is owned by the StEvent framework
(\c St_DataSet / \c StXRefMain).

\warning Do **not** delete individual \ref StPxlHit pointers obtained from the
collection.  The collection manages their lifetimes.

\section pxl_members Data Members

\subsection pxl_members_top StPxlHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StPxlSectorHitCollection[10]` | `mSectors` | Fixed-size array of 10 sector sub-collections. |

\subsection pxl_members_sector StPxlSectorHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StPxlLadderHitCollection[4]` | `mLadders` | Fixed-size array of 4 ladder sub-collections per sector. |

\subsection pxl_members_ladder StPxlLadderHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StPxlSensorHitCollection[10]` | `mSensors` | Fixed-size array of 10 sensor sub-collections per ladder. |

\subsection pxl_members_sensor StPxlSensorHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StSPtrVecPxlHit` | `mHits` | Smart-pointer vector of `StPxlHit*`; owns all contained hits. |

\section pxl_methods Key Methods

\subsection pxl_methods_top StPxlHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `addHit(StPxlHit*)` | `bool` | Routes hit to correct sector/ladder/sensor. Returns `false` if any index is out of range. |
| `numberOfHits() const` | `unsigned int` | Total hits across all sectors, ladders, and sensors. |
| `numberOfSectors() const` | `unsigned int` | Always 10. |
| `sector(unsigned int)` | `StPxlSectorHitCollection*` | 0-based sector access; returns `nullptr` if out of range. |

\subsection pxl_methods_sector StPxlSectorHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `numberOfHits() const` | `unsigned int` | Total hits in this sector. |
| `numberOfLadders() const` | `unsigned int` | Always 4. |
| `ladder(unsigned int)` | `StPxlLadderHitCollection*` | 0-based ladder access; returns `nullptr` if out of range. |

\subsection pxl_methods_ladder StPxlLadderHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `numberOfHits() const` | `unsigned int` | Total hits on this ladder. |
| `numberOfSensors() const` | `unsigned int` | Always 10. |
| `sensor(unsigned int)` | `StPxlSensorHitCollection*` | 0-based sensor access; returns `nullptr` if out of range. |

\subsection pxl_methods_sensor StPxlSensorHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `hits()` | `StSPtrVecPxlHit&` | Mutable reference to the hit vector. |
| `hits() const` | `const StSPtrVecPxlHit&` | Const reference to the hit vector. |

\section pxl_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StPxlHitCollection* pxlColl = event->pxlHitCollection();
if (!pxlColl) return;

for (unsigned int iSec = 0; iSec < pxlColl->numberOfSectors(); ++iSec) {
    const StPxlSectorHitCollection* secColl = pxlColl->sector(iSec);
    if (!secColl) continue;

    for (unsigned int iLad = 0; iLad < secColl->numberOfLadders(); ++iLad) {
        const StPxlLadderHitCollection* ladColl = secColl->ladder(iLad);
        if (!ladColl) continue;

        for (unsigned int iSen = 0; iSen < ladColl->numberOfSensors(); ++iSen) {
            const StPxlSensorHitCollection* senColl = ladColl->sensor(iSen);
            if (!senColl) continue;

            const StSPtrVecPxlHit& hits = senColl->hits();
            for (const StPxlHit* hit : hits) {
                // process hit ...
            }
        }
    }
}
\endcode
*/
